devel/ -- published, but never going to qemu-devel
==================================================

Patches needed by anyone who builds or modifies sun4v firmware against QEMU, and
by nobody else. They are published (mirrored to github.com/unix0cc/qemu-experimental
under devel/) because they are useful to others doing the same work, but they are
not proposed upstream and are not written to upstream's standards for inclusion.

Contrast with the sibling directories:

  upstream/  posted or intended for qemu-devel; numbered as a series; must stay
             byte-identical to the published copy
  devel/     this directory; same byte-identity rule
  test/      experiment-local, never published, deleted when the experiment ends

The byte-identity rule matters: the published copy is the canonical location of a
patch, and a local edit that is not mirrored makes the two silently disagree.
Regenerate SHA256SUMS after editing anything here.

Contents
--------
niagara-hvuart-console.patch
    Models the hypervisor's private console UART at 0xfff0c2c000, an address the
    machine's own hv MD has always declared (`hvuart` in the root node) and which
    QEMU did not decode. Required to run a self-built hypervisor at all: such a
    build hangs on its first PRINT(). Harmless to existing setups -- the stock
    blob is a non-DEBUG build and writes nothing to the port.
